<title>NETHERLANDS: Simac buys Belgium's Netbuilding.</title>
<headline>Simac buys Belgium's Netbuilding.</headline>
<dateline>VELDHOVEN, Netherlands 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch computer services and engineering firm Simac Techniek NV said on Monday it had agreed to buy Netbuilding Europe NV in Belgium.</p>
<p>The deal, of which no financial details were given, also includes Netbuilding's subsidiary in the Czech Republic and a 50 percent stake in the Dutch unit Netbuilding Nederland.</p>
<p>Netbuilding designs, installs and operates large-scale networks for data and telecommunications. The company expects to post 1997 turnover of about 50 million guilders and has more than 100 employees.</p>
<p>Simac said it would include Netbuilding's figures in its own results from July 1997.</p>
<p>It added its profit and loss account would include a write-off for paid goodwill, so that the takeover would have a neutral to slightly positive effect on this year's earnings per share.</p>
